  "question": {
    "text": "A particle is moving in a straight line. At time $t$, the distance between the particle from its starting point is given by $x=t-6 t+z$. Its acceleration will be zero at",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "yjzgs",
      "text": "$t=1$ unit time",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Agef7",
      "text": "$t=2$ unit time",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "NaLPg",
      "text": "$t=3$ unit time",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Sxl3e",
      "text": "$t=4$ unit time",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints : $x=t-6 t^2+t^3$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{d x}{d t}=1-12 t+3 t^2 \\\\\n& \\frac{d^2 x}{d t^2}=-12+6 t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nAcceleration $=\\frac{d^2 x}{d t^2}$\n$\\therefore$ Acceleration $=0 \\Rightarrow 6 t-12=0 \\Rightarrow t=2$",
    "image": null
  },
